arger squares and you also have  these two excess sheets so just grab the  green sheet take the top right corner  again and fold it across to the left so  that you line up the top and the left  edges make a crease and then all you  need to do is to remove this little  triangular area by taking off the excess  paper when you do that you'll come up  with your smallest piece now you have  the two largest squares and the smallest  square completed to make the last two  squares grab your last  sheet of green printer paper take the  top and fold it down to the bottom line  up the edges and then make a crease  along the top edge all you need to do  now is to rip the paper in half because  we only need half of the sheet once you  do that you'll get two sheets just like  this now just grab one of them because  you just need half and you're going to  do the same thing we've been doing take  the upper right corner fold it across to  the left and then you could remove the  excess paper so here I've already made  the creases so let's rip the paper and  then all you need to do so here you have  one square and you know what to do with  this excess sheet so just take the  corner fold it across and then remove  the excess paper on the bottom when  you're done you'll have five square  sheets just like the ones I showed now  I'm going to show you how to fold the  top four pieces of the tree which I made  the exact same way except they're  different sizes  grab your largest square we've already  folded it this way you want to take the  upper left corner now and fold it down  to the bottom right corner line up the  edges and make crease  unfold the paper and you'll see you have  an X in it take the top edge and fold it  down to the bottom edge and once they're  lined up make a crease when you unfold  it you'll see you now have a horizontal  line so we want to fold the left edge  over to the right edge now so if you do  want to flip it or turn it like this now  you could take the top and fold it down  to the bottom again make a crease now if  you unfold the paper you'll see you have  an X and also a cross in the paper turn  the paper like this and we're going to  fold the corner of the paper over to the  other corner on one of these diagonal  lines just like that so that we have a  triangle with the tip on the bottom hold  the paper and lift up the first layer  here and we're going to tuck this right  corner down towards the tip of the  triangle here  lift up the first layer and tuck this  corner inwards just like that then just  flatten everything out do the same with  the left side hold the paper here on the  right lift up this first layer tuck the  corner in and then flatten everything  out now we have this diamond structure  which is similar to the bird base we're  going to start making all of the pieces  of the origami tree with this diamond  even the base of the tree so you need to  remember how to make this what we're  going to do now is if you'll notice we  have four points here on the bottom now  we're going to take each one of those  points and fold them up to the top of  the diamond so start off with the one  here on the front grab this first layer  of paper and fold this point up to the  top like this once it's lined up make a  crease along the bottom now just flip  the paper over and do the same with this  point on the bottom take the corner fold  it up to the top and just make a crease  on the bottom  so now we just have two left now you'll  see its flattened out this way so what  you want to do is you want to hold it on  the side like this going to open these  two flaps on the front open the two  flaps on the back like this and then  flatten it out this way so just flatten  it this way now and now you'll see we  could just fold up these two points like  we did before so fold it up and make a  crease along the bottom flip it over and  do the same thing with the other side  now you should have something that looks  just like this okay 