're going  to open this this slot here and push on  this edge so you want to push on this  edge like that take the tip round it off  like this and just roll it right into  there and make sure it's folding here on  this corner so you should be able to  kind of work it all the way in there and  push it in and then you'll see you want  to pop this back so just push here on  this edge now I know it's tricky but if  you practice it a little bit and make  sure that you're opening the paper  enough and rolling that in there you  should be able to get it okay so there  you go you have finished your piece now  that you know how to make one piece you  can go on to make the remaining top  pieces they do become a little bit  trickier as you go smaller and smaller  so if you're finding yourself getting  frustrated or having a little bit of  trouble don't worry about it all you  need to do is just make a couple of the  larger ones and your tree will still  come out looking pretty good however  you'll see that if you do practice a  little bit even with the smallest piece  you should be able to tuck everything in  and then finally get that last piece in  there  all that's left to do now is to fold the  base of the tree and as I said before  you're going to need one of these  diamond shapes for every single piece so  once you have one of these make sure  that you're holding the open end on the  bottom just like this with all of these  little tips facing down  then all we're going to do is take the  two top flaps and we're going to fold  these edges into the midline set it down  on the table take this top edge and fold  it in to the midline and make a crease  do the same with the other top flap take  this edge and fold it in you should have  something that looks just like this flip  it over and do the same with the other  two flaps just fold the right edge onto  the midline make a crease and do the  same with the left side from here on  you'll see that making the base is very  similar to making the green pieces the  only difference is that we don't fold  these little corners or tips all the way  up to the top what we're going to do  instead is just take the tip pull it  upwards until it can't go any more which  is basically along this edge and then  make a crease along the bottom flip it  over and do the same exact thing with  this tip just fold it up and then make a  crease on the bottom so now we're going  to do the same thing that we did before  turn it to the side open these front  flaps and open the back flaps and then  just squash it in this direction now now  you can take these two tips on the  bottom and fold it up all the way just  like this and make a crease  from here on making the base is exactly  the same as making the green pieces so  I'm going to speed up the video but I'll  still narrate and let you know what I'm  doing so we're going to pinch the tip  and fold it to the right and then crease  down the middle do the same thing for  the next one pinch the edges together  fold it to the right and then crease  down the middle do the same thing for  the last one  so now you have all these flaps and you  want to fold them to the left now so  that they're going in a clockwise  direction do that for all four of the  flaps and then you could tuck them in  one there's the second one  here's the third one and then the fourth  one that's a little tricky so just round  off the tip and roll it in there push on  that edge so that you open up the slot  and you should be able to kind of work  it in there so that it locks completely  and there you go there's your base now  that you've finished all the pieces just  grab the base and you'll see that these  four edges sticking up can fit into any  of the four slots on the bottom of the  pieces so all you need to do is to just  line them up and then you could slide it  in do the same with the next piece  and there you go there's your origami  tree I hope you enjoyed my tutorial for  the origami tree